    "user_request_original": "Design and optimize a 26-layer planar dielectric multilayer coating on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Materials: HfO2 (high index) and SiO2 (low index), alternating sequence starting with HfO2 adjacent to air. Initialize layer thicknesses using quadratic chirp formula: d_i = d_0 * (1 + alpha * (i-1)^2) where d_0 = 75 nm for HfO2 layers and 110 nm for SiO2 layers, alpha = 0.003. Then perform gradient-based thickness optimization with bound constraints: each thickness may vary ±12% from its initialized value. Wavelength range: 300-1700 nm with 5 nm sampling. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized light. Objective: maximize weighted spectral performance score with equal weight on (1) average reflectance in 300-450 nm band and (2) average transmittance in 1000-1700 nm band. Report best candidate thicknesses, target score, robustness score, and full spectral curves. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 300-450 nm, 1000-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1000-1700 nm; high reflection in 300-450 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: reflection in 1000-1700 nm; transmission in 300-450 nm. manufacturing constraints: Maximum total layer count of 30.",
